1
00:00:00,123 --> 00:00:01,483
A prince saves the beauty.

2
00:00:03,143 --> 00:00:10,223
Is that a cliché?
It seems a bit clichéd to me.

3
00:00:11,163 --> 00:00:12,463
Let's try something less clichéd.

4
00:00:20,183 --> 00:00:25,943
Just now—that wasn't clichéd.

5
00:00:25,943 --> 00:00:31,583
But if he bends down to carry me,
it might not look good.

6
00:00:31,583 --> 00:00:37,323
You're thinking about so much.
An actor with a director's mindset.

7
00:00:37,323 --> 00:00:38,663
I've met actors like that before.

8
00:00:40,663 --> 00:00:41,743
I'm like that too.

9
00:00:43,743 --> 00:00:45,223
I've realized I shouldn't be.

10
00:00:49,563 --> 00:00:53,683
Even when I'm acting for you,
I can't help worrying about everything.

11
00:00:55,443 --> 00:00:59,843
You have to trust your collaborators.
Take this light, for example.

12
00:01:00,107 --> 00:01:05,107
Don't worry about it.
You don't need to think about the film.

13
00:01:05,607 --> 00:01:10,627
Just do what you most want to do
as the characters in the script.

14
00:01:10,627 --> 00:01:12,687
Give me a piece of ice, please.
Okay.

15
00:01:24,227 --> 00:01:25,527
Why are you thinking about it?

16
00:01:27,267 --> 00:01:29,947
This ice isn't big enough.
Forget it. Let it go.

17
00:01:32,027 --> 00:01:36,627
Wait. I keep breaking character.
Sorry.

18
00:01:36,627 --> 00:01:43,147
It's okay. Break character if you need to.
You can always come back into it.

19
00:01:43,147 --> 00:01:48,027
Does this look good?
I'm always thinking about that...

20
00:01:48,907 --> 00:01:53,907
I'm thinking about
where we begin and where we end.

21
00:01:55,067 --> 00:01:57,147
You think about it. I'll think about it.

22
00:02:00,847 --> 00:02:04,107
The beginning...
or what you have in your script.

23
00:02:06,007 --> 00:02:11,747
You're destroying me. It begins
when I realize you're destroying me.

24
00:02:11,747 --> 00:02:16,407
Then I'm destroyed, and you rest.
You're cold, until you freeze to death.

25
00:02:17,587 --> 00:02:20,727
That's bleak.
A dark beginning and a dark ending.

26
00:02:21,927 --> 00:02:26,187
Let's play it naturally, not theatrically.
Understood. I know.

27
00:02:27,067 --> 00:02:30,547
But everyday life has emotion
and violence too.

28
00:02:30,841 --> 00:02:35,681
Looking at you makes me want to laugh.
Why? Should I do comedy?

29
00:02:36,701 --> 00:02:38,941
No, that's not what I mean.

30
00:02:50,681 --> 00:02:55,881
Seeing someone you like
makes you want to smile.

31
00:02:55,881 --> 00:02:59,981
I don't feel like smiling that often.

32
00:03:00,533 --> 00:03:02,553
I don't feel like you're destroying me.

33
00:03:09,473 --> 00:03:11,353
Used to it.
Used to what?

34
00:03:14,793 --> 00:03:16,233
Hurting people.

35
00:03:17,573 --> 00:03:20,353
Because I wrote it
when I was in a bad mood.

36
00:03:22,153 --> 00:03:23,453
It's actually pretty good.

37
00:03:27,193 --> 00:03:30,393
Maybe we don't hurt each other.
Maybe there's tenderness.

38
00:03:31,253 --> 00:03:34,213
A kind of helpless love.
